.TH FIRSTSPARK 1 "2026-09-26" "firstspark 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
firstspark \- Cheat Engine style memory scanner, debugger and code patcher
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B firstspark
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B firstspark
attaches to a running process as an unprivileged user, scans its memory for
values, lets you filter and edit the results, browses and patches machine code,
and scales time inside the target process. It needs no Python or GDB runtime
dependency.
.PP
With neither
.B \-list
nor
.B \-pid
it opens the graphical interface. The GUI mirrors the Cheat Engine layout: a
scan panel and Found list, a cheat table, a separate Memory Viewer and a
Debugger window, a Lua Engine console, and settings under Edit.
.PP
Supplying
.B \-pid
runs a headless scan and prints the results to standard output.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-config " FILE"
Read configuration from
.IR FILE .
Defaults to
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/firstspark/config.yaml .
.TP
.B \-list
List the visible processes (PID, UID, name, command line) and exit.
.TP
.BI \-pid " PID"
Target process id for a headless scan.
.TP
.BI \-type " TYPE"
Value type to scan for: one of
.IR byte ", " word ", " dword ", " qword ", " float ", " double ", " string ,
.IR aob ", " binary ", " all " or " grouped ,
or the name of a user-defined type.
.TP
.BI \-mode " MODE"
Scan mode:
.IR exact ", " bigger ", " smaller ", " between ", " unknown ,
.IR increased ", " increased\ by ", " decreased ", " decreased\ by ,
.IR changed ", " unchanged " or " same\ as\ first .
.TP
.BI \-value " VALUE"
Value to scan for. Numeric types accept decimal, hexadecimal
.RB ( 0x
prefix) or an expression; grouped types use
.RI type:value
segments such as
.RB ` 4:75 " " 4:* " " 4:100 `.
.TP
.BI \-value2 " VALUE"
Upper bound for a
.B between
scan.
.TP
.BI \-compare " OP"
Comparison operator for an exact scan:
.IR == ", " != ", " > ", " >= ", " < " or " <= .
.TP
.BI \-next " MODE"
Run a next scan with this mode before printing results.
.TP
.BI \-exec " FILTER"
Restrict regions by executable permission:
.IR any ", " only " or " non .
.TP
.B \-cow
Scan only copy-on-write (private) regions.
.TP
.BI \-start " ADDR"
Lower bound of the scan range, in hexadecimal.
.TP
.BI \-stop " ADDR"
Upper bound of the scan range, in hexadecimal.
.TP
.BI \-export " FILE"
Write the results to
.IR FILE .
The format follows the extension:
.IR .ct " (XML), " .json " or " .yaml .
.TP
.BI \-log-level " LEVEL"
Log level:
.IR debug ", " info ", " warn " or " error .
.TP
.B \-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
List the target candidates:
.PP
.RS 4
.B firstspark \-list
.RE
.PP
Find a 4-byte value and narrow it after it increases:
.PP
.RS 4
.B firstspark \-pid 1234 \-type dword \-mode unknown \-next increased
.RE
.PP
Scan a grouped structure and export it as YAML:
.PP
.RS 4
.B firstspark \-pid 1234 \-type grouped \-value "4:75 4:* 4:100" \-export run.yaml
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/firstspark/config.yaml
Configuration; see
.I configs/config.yaml
in the source tree for the defaults.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/firstspark/customtypes.yaml
User-defined value types.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/firstspark/
Saved scan sessions and cheat tables.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/firstspark/firstspark.log
Diagnostic log.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME, XDG_DATA_HOME, XDG_STATE_HOME, XDG_CACHE_HOME
Base directories for configuration, data, state and cache.
.TP
.B DISPLAY
X11 display used by the GUI and by the global-hotkey backend.
.TP
.B FYNE_SCALE
Interface scale factor, read by Fyne at startup.
.TP
.B FIRSTSPARK_ORIG_UID, FIRSTSPARK_ORIG_GID, SUDO_UID, SUDO_GID
Used when running elevated so files stay owned by the invoking user.
.SH NOTES
Attaching requires the kernel to permit it:
.I kernel.yama.ptrace_scope=0
or
.BR CAP_SYS_PTRACE .
Speedhack and the unrandomizer hook libc time and random functions; calls served
directly by the vDSO bypass the speedhack.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gdb (1),
.BR proc (5)
